{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q320603","formula":"TiO₂","hill":"O2Ti","elements":["O","Ti"],"composition":{"O":2.0,"Ti":1.0},"names":{"en":"Rutile","ru":"Рутил","uk":"Рутил"},"descriptions":{"en":"Rutile is an oxide mineral composed of titanium dioxide (TiO2), and is the most common natural form of TiO2. Rarer polymorphs of TiO2 are known, including anatase, akaogiite, and brookite. Rutile has one of the highest refractive indices at visible wavelengths of any known crystal and also exhibits a particularly large birefringence and high dispersion.","ru":"Рути́л (от лат. rutilus — изжелта-красный, золотисто-красный) — минерал класса оксидов, наиболее распространённая полиморфная модификация диоксида титана TiO2 (наряду c брукитом и анатазом). Изоморфные примеси: Cr, Nb, Ta, V, Sn.","uk":"Рутил (англ. rutile; нім. Rutil) — мінерал класу оксидів та гідрооксидів; діоксид титану ланцюжкової будови."},"fame":53,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-390","atoms":31,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[3.783,0.0,0.0],[0.0,3.783,0.0],[0.0,0.0,9.615]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":1.891,"y":1.891,"z":4.808,"el":"Ti"},{"x":1.891,"y":0.0,"z":7.211,"el":"Ti"},{"x":1.891,"y":3.783,"z":7.211,"el":"Ti"},{"x":0.0,"y":1.891,"z":4.396,"el":"O"},{"x":3.783,"y":1.891,"z":4.396,"el":"O"},{"x":1.891,"y":1.891,"z":6.799,"el":"O"},{"x":1.891,"y":0.0,"z":5.219,"el":"O"},{"x":1.891,"y":3.783,"z":5.219,"el":"O"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":7.623,"el":"O"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.783,"z":7.623,"el":"O"},{"x":3.783,"y":0.0,"z":7.623,"el":"O"},{"x":3.783,"y":3.783,"z":7.623,"el":"O"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Ti"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":9.615,"el":"Ti"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.783,"z":0.0,"el":"Ti"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.783,"z":9.615,"el":"Ti"},{"x":3.783,